    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose 80.07 score makes him our premier start. Facing Ryan Gusto, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a premium spot at the top of the lineup; while we anticipate a slight drag due to his high SB-potential being neutralized by a tough hold, his xwOBA profile makes him our most efficient engine today. Close behind is **Yordan Alvarez** (73.11), who remains a must-start despite facing a formidable arm in George Kirby. The elite xwOBA metrics for **Yordan Alvarez** provide enough insulation against the SP skill factor to maintain his status as a lineup pillar.\n\nStrategic gains are being driven primarily by dynamic platoon advantages. **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (69.90) are both capitalizing on favorable park factors against Bassitt and Scherzer, respectively, with **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** specifically seeing a 16% park-driven boost that offsets his neutral platoon profile. Conversely, **Trea Turner** (47.38) presents a risk-reward scenario; despite his elite speed, the combination of a daunting matchup against Logan Henderson and a negative 19% SP skill impact forces a lower efficiency score than his pedigree might suggest. Regarding the bench, **Carson Benge** (51.63) was the hardest omission. He narrowly missed the cut due to the optimization of platoon-heavy roles elsewhere, as the system prioritized the higher park-adjusted floors provided by **Josh Smith** and **Lars Nootbaar**.\n\nOwners should monitor the final lineups closely, as many of today\u2019s slots\u2014including **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Christian Yelich**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Yordan Alvarez**, and **Junior Caminero**\u2014are currently relying on assumed batting positions. A significant shift in the order could ripple through our daily efficiency. Furthermore, we are tracking wind-in conditions, which have prompted a 5% negative adjustment across several slots, adding a subtle layer of volatility to the power projections for players like **Gary Sanchez** and **Chase Meidroth**. Ensure that **Colt Keith** remains on the bench as he navigates his IL status.",
